          "name": "InfectX: Pathogen infection siRNA screens",
          "description": [
            "Pathogen infection siRNA screens for Bartonella henselae, Brucella abortus and Salmonella typhimurium performed within the InfectX consortium (http://www.infectx.ch)."
          ],
          "protocol": [
            "Below, we sketch out the assay protocol. Detailed description can be found in Ramo et al., 2014 and Schmich et al., 2015.",
            "",
            "Cell culture:",
            "Experiments were performed in HeLa CCL-2 (ATCC) cells.",
            "",
            "siRNA transfection and infection:",
            "We used various commercially available siRNA libraries from Ambion, Dharmacon and Qiagen of different scale (genome and kinome wide) and structure (single and pooled). All experiments were conducted in a 384-well plate format. After transfection, pathogen was added to wells.",
            "",
            "Imaging:",
            "Cells were stained for DNA, F-actin and infection specific markers and imaged on Molecular Devices ImageXpress microscopes.",
            "",
            "Phenotyping:",
            "Infectivity phenotypes were derived using CellProfiler from image data. We removed outlier wells, normalized for row and column effects using B scoring from Brideau et al. and scaled by median absolute deviation."
          ],
